{"id": "EUVD-2026-103941", "enisaUuid": "af944c4a-4d73-3995-9f32-05274763f563", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nthunderbolt: Reject oversized XDomain properties responses\n\ntb_xdp_properties_request() allocates room for 45 data dwords in its\n252-byte response buffer.  The XDomain length field is six bits wide,\nhowever, and a malicious peer can set it to 63.  After the fixed response\nfields are subtracted, the driver treats this as 48 data dwords.\n\nCommit 322e93448d90 (\"thunderbolt: Clamp XDomain response data copy to\nallocation size\") only bounds the copy against data_len.  If data_len is\nat least 48, memcpy() reads 192 bytes from the 180-byte res->data array,\ncausing a 12-byte heap out-of-bounds read.  Commit 4db2bd2ed478\n(\"thunderbolt: Limit XDomain response copy to actual frame size\") limits\nthe earlier copy but does not constrain this header-derived length.\n\nReject response data lengths that exceed the allocated source buffer\nbefore copying them into the assembled property block.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:45:58", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:55:42", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b270c1074860de74da0d6b5250fb06b359b9d509", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a766a86ff48acee76aeb8e2575771040749e509d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2f97f929dad9eb3e1f63b721d2dd49bf9bc68efa", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/737a1d2e9642d5f718bd29aa4a98b9eef3832f0a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/80756e263846ab694984e749e8c626897331438f"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98687", "GHSA-rq3j-rw4p-w59w"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1ce76308-b4df-3942-a17a-06d20cedecea", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.56"}, {"id": "403a6760-959e-3ec0-99db-41ef934ac9bb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4.15"}, {"id": "40908f18-1310-313d-942c-346749652d68", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d1ff70241a275133e1a0258b7c23588b122276c8 <737a1d2e9642d5f718bd29aa4a98b9eef3832f0a"}, {"id": "48b7f595-3fa8-3fb1-a57b-6c1eb346611a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "4e974a28-d2b5-3eeb-ba2a-f193715e3659", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d1ff70241a275133e1a0258b7c23588b122276c8 <b270c1074860de74da0d6b5250fb06b359b9d509"}, {"id": "726dbf30-7a43-39ff-8aff-05003436d415", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "85c6cd08-c14c-398c-bce8-dbce0dfb949e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.10"}, {"id": "8fa203c3-51c0-31fe-87af-a26803886ec2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d1ff70241a275133e1a0258b7c23588b122276c8 <2f97f929dad9eb3e1f63b721d2dd49bf9bc68efa"}, {"id": "92d99116-61e9-3998-9c52-998d2f42ce6d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "b033f791-ed5b-3103-ac29-88454f38abd7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d1ff70241a275133e1a0258b7c23588b122276c8 <80756e263846ab694984e749e8c626897331438f"}, {"id": "c98e19ee-f0c6-3b80-833f-778cc32e2c84", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.113"}, {"id": "db10fc29-8b6c-3b8c-8785-8e8533ab0d6f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d1ff70241a275133e1a0258b7c23588b122276c8 <a766a86ff48acee76aeb8e2575771040749e509d"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "dff1bf9c-f177-31be-b6b5-1300b5a50793", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}